01:13:57.920 --> 01:14:03.920
governing, as in mankind, governing the mind, you look into nature.

01:14:03.920 --> 01:14:11.920
Enter nature, eventually you hold, some of you, to which God?

01:14:11.920 --> 01:14:18.920
From man, nature, God.

01:14:18.920 --> 01:14:22.920
That is the goal of life.

01:14:22.920 --> 01:14:28.520
Man, nature, and eventually...

01:14:28.520 --> 01:14:30.720
God.

01:14:30.720 --> 01:14:33.720
The Jewish way is different.

01:14:33.720 --> 01:14:38.320
Rashi Chokhmah, we understand.

01:14:38.320 --> 01:14:41.520
We come to nature via God.

01:14:41.520 --> 01:14:45.720
We recognize God.

01:14:45.720 --> 01:14:49.920
And through God, we understand nature.

01:14:49.920 --> 01:14:55.760
The Rashi Barah Elohim Eritaz Hamaim Beit Ha'aretz

01:14:55.760 --> 01:15:01.320
We understand nature after accepting God.

01:15:01.320 --> 01:15:04.800
We understand nature through God.

01:15:04.800 --> 01:15:08.520
Rashi Chokmah in Adonai.

01:15:08.520 --> 01:15:10.480
How could you say this in different words?

01:15:10.480 --> 01:15:13.920
Atah Honein Le'adam Da'at

01:15:13.920 --> 01:15:18.320
God comes from you or via your God.

01:15:18.320 --> 01:15:20.020
You understand?

01:15:20.020 --> 01:15:26.720
Very deep, very profound, very precise statement.

01:15:26.720 --> 01:15:33.320
The God, the Knowledge, you know, there is your gift,

01:15:33.320 --> 01:15:38.020
but only could come according to our point of view,

01:15:38.020 --> 01:15:41.520
after accepting God and through God.

01:15:41.520 --> 01:15:59.400
This is the purpose of how to see man, God, nature. How is it to be seen? Two ways. The goal. Man looks into nature and from nature he discovers God. Jewish way. Man looks into God and through God he discovers nature.

01:15:59.400 --> 01:16:13.400
Tachonem le'edam da'at. Clear? What does it mean the word da'at? We'll see later on.

01:16:13.400 --> 01:16:22.400
And you teach to men, binah. I explain to you what I mean, binah.

01:16:22.400 --> 01:16:29.400
We have onneno meiteka, and we are begging of you, begging ourselves, we don't merit it.

01:16:29.400 --> 01:16:37.400
There was a person who studied ten hours, and accomplished less than a person who studies half an hour.

01:16:37.400 --> 01:16:50.400
This is the question of a name. That is the gift of God. And I'm going to tell you what's the importance of this. In America, I found the importance of it.

01:16:50.400 --> 01:17:01.400
So, Einstein made his most important discoveries in his 20s, after the age of 26, 27, he made all his discoveries.

01:17:01.400 --> 01:17:09.400
Everything from the age of 26, 27 until the end of his life was his discovery zero.

01:17:09.400 --> 01:17:13.400
Now, you may say that Einstein was very stupid or was more stupid.

01:17:13.400 --> 01:17:15.400
What's the question of?

01:17:15.400 --> 01:17:17.400
Chonenu!

01:17:17.400 --> 01:17:19.400
God didn't inspire him.

01:17:19.400 --> 01:17:24.400
How could be that after the age of 26 he was so dead and after the nachi?

01:17:24.400 --> 01:17:28.400
We don't know. That's one of the miracles of the idea of chonenu rabda'at.

01:17:31.400 --> 01:17:34.400
L'chamnenu me'itecha, we beg of you.

01:17:36.400 --> 01:17:40.400
Chochma b'nar wada'at.

01:17:40.400 --> 01:17:43.120
Ha'vashem, onen atah.

01:17:43.380 --> 01:17:45.820
Blessed are those that do good things.

01:17:46.440 --> 01:17:47.460
So what does it mean to say,

01:17:47.680 --> 01:17:49.760
Chokmah, minah, badah?

01:17:51.200 --> 01:17:53.440
Let me tell you how I understand this.

01:17:55.380 --> 01:17:56.400
Chokmah is wisdom.

01:17:56.980 --> 01:17:57.720
I don't know how you do it.

01:17:57.760 --> 01:17:59.220
You don't know how you do it.

01:17:59.960 --> 01:18:01.280
But the idea is the following.

01:18:02.500 --> 01:18:04.900
Chakram is a person

01:18:04.900 --> 01:18:07.360
who thinks a thought

01:18:07.360 --> 01:18:10.300
for first time

01:18:10.300 --> 01:18:12.300
in the history of mankind.

01:18:17.300 --> 01:18:21.300
If you think something that nobody else has thought before,

01:18:23.300 --> 01:18:25.300
that is a hard thing.

01:18:27.300 --> 01:18:28.300
No.

01:18:28.300 --> 01:18:30.300
PhDs, I give PhDs.

01:18:31.300 --> 01:18:33.300
There is no PhD thesis.

01:18:34.300 --> 01:18:36.300
But think an original thought.

01:18:37.300 --> 01:18:38.300
There is no thesis.

01:18:38.300 --> 01:18:47.300
There are very few people in the history of mankind who think an original thought for the first time in the history of mankind.

01:18:47.300 --> 01:18:56.300
Very well. Here's an example. Take for instance Galileo.

01:18:56.300 --> 01:19:03.300
That all the humans are simulating, not comparable.

01:19:03.300 --> 01:19:13.300
He sees the sun, the planets, the stars. What he sees, what he saw rather, is what every other Earth is going on.

01:19:13.300 --> 01:19:23.300
All of a sudden, it feels like this. Everybody assumes that the Earth is in the middle and everything is going wrong.

01:19:23.300 --> 01:19:27.300
There were many questions that nobody was able to answer.

01:19:27.300 --> 01:19:30.300
But, and you can hear.

01:19:30.300 --> 01:19:33.300
Maybe the Earth is not in the center.

01:19:33.300 --> 01:19:38.300
Maybe the Earth is going around the Sun.

01:19:38.300 --> 01:19:40.300
That's the original idea.

01:19:40.300 --> 01:19:42.300
It's the same data.

01:19:42.300 --> 01:19:44.300
What we think is the original idea.

01:19:44.300 --> 01:19:46.300
What we think is Einstein.

01:19:46.300 --> 01:19:48.300
The problems that there were before,

01:19:48.300 --> 01:19:50.300
that Einstein tried to solve,

01:19:50.300 --> 01:19:52.300
And how do everybody recognize?

01:19:53.300 --> 01:19:58.300
Things to do with the speed of light, things to do with the gravity, things to do with the elliptic...

01:19:59.300 --> 01:20:03.300
things of the stars and the moon, the elliptic orbits.

01:20:04.300 --> 01:20:06.300
Everybody saw it, everybody found it.

01:20:06.300 --> 01:20:11.300
Or somebody has a way to see reality in a different way.

01:20:12.300 --> 01:20:16.300
If there's something new to it, then others, you know, same, same, same.

01:20:16.300 --> 01:20:19.780
you know, each one, he sees the same thing that you see,

01:20:19.780 --> 01:20:21.440
here's a different word.

01:20:22.020 --> 01:20:26.720
What is interesting about the Hakan is that after he points this to you and says,

01:20:27.020 --> 01:20:32.240
of course, I've known it all the time, it's obvious.

01:20:33.580 --> 01:20:33.860
You see?

01:20:34.620 --> 01:20:36.340
Let me give you a wrong example.

01:20:36.680 --> 01:20:37.500
What is an example?

01:20:37.860 --> 01:20:40.940
I mean, because it's historically untrue and all those things.

01:20:41.240 --> 01:20:43.880
But let me give you an example with Columbus.

01:20:43.880 --> 01:20:46.880
That's the Dalai, probably done two or three.

01:20:46.880 --> 01:20:54.880
You know what he said about going to the east via west.

01:20:54.880 --> 01:20:57.880
To the India, which was in the east via the west.

01:20:57.880 --> 01:21:01.880
So he says, could you take this egg and make it stand up?

01:21:01.880 --> 01:21:02.880
Nobody was able to.

01:21:02.880 --> 01:21:04.880
He crushed it and the egg stand up.

01:21:04.880 --> 01:21:05.880
You know?

01:21:05.880 --> 01:21:08.880
So after he questioned, he said, of course, it's obvious.

01:21:08.880 --> 01:21:16.880
I could make it a story or play the story about the Chagam, very brief.

01:21:16.880 --> 01:21:23.880
To people who don't, I like the story. You know, and I always, when I have the opportunity, I say it.

01:21:23.880 --> 01:21:31.880
Alright? It is of course about one of the persons that I identify with very much, and I'm in great

01:21:31.880 --> 01:21:36.920
I'm in great admire of him and I study his work very carefully as much as I can.

01:21:36.920 --> 01:21:38.840
This is Maran Akalos, ala basharot.

01:21:38.840 --> 01:21:45.640
You know, Maran is the author of Shukran Ayut, the most important book for halakha,

01:21:45.640 --> 01:21:50.040
that we have, the paladin of Spetanim, that's the ultimate work in halakha.

01:21:50.040 --> 01:21:58.520
Now, the legend goes to say that he used to have a young Nari that came once in a while

01:21:58.520 --> 01:22:02.520
and studying together was a mischnio.

01:22:02.520 --> 01:22:06.520
No, I don't think it was a mischnio.

01:22:06.520 --> 01:22:10.520
So it was a mischnio.

01:22:10.520 --> 01:22:14.520
That's a mischnio.

01:22:18.520 --> 01:22:22.520
And Maran has all his colleagues.

01:22:22.520 --> 01:22:24.520
knowledge.

01:22:24.520 --> 01:22:26.520
We have the

01:22:26.520 --> 01:22:28.520
Rani, the Yaakov, the Yeruah,

01:22:28.520 --> 01:22:30.520
Yaakov, the U'athia, all this great

01:22:30.520 --> 01:22:32.520
knowledge. None of them was able

01:22:32.520 --> 01:22:34.520
to do that.

01:22:38.520 --> 01:22:40.520
Mind the science

01:22:40.520 --> 01:22:42.520
since there was no human being who could

01:22:42.520 --> 01:22:44.520
help him. But next time when the young

01:22:44.520 --> 01:22:46.520
one arrived, it was not to him. It was to

01:22:46.520 --> 01:22:48.520
Chayot. It was not to

01:22:48.520 --> 01:22:50.520
anyone. What was to his parents and

01:22:50.520 --> 01:23:00.520
So, you meet, and Yavan Hare says, what's the meaning of the task?

01:23:00.520 --> 01:23:09.520
And Yavan Hare says, and I think that was a good, you should know, that you are the first human being who will interpret this, this, this thing.

01:23:09.520 --> 01:23:15.520
Nobody before you, this was in the heavens, this, this, and then, then, then, the meaning, and you brought the task to Earth.

01:23:15.520 --> 01:23:17.520
Yes.

01:23:17.520 --> 01:23:19.520
You are the first.

01:23:19.520 --> 01:23:21.520
But I was very happy,

01:23:21.520 --> 01:23:28.520
besides to go to the Red Midrash and share that interpretation with his colleagues.

01:23:28.520 --> 01:23:34.520
He goes on the stairs. If you ever go to Sauteuil, you go to see Le Marant,

01:23:34.520 --> 01:23:38.520
they live downstairs and there is the Red Midrash upstairs.

01:23:38.520 --> 01:23:39.520
Right?

01:23:39.520 --> 01:23:44.520
So, he goes up the stairs and he enters the Red Midrash.

01:23:44.520 --> 01:23:50.520
I remember as a child, he sees a little boy, about 6 or 7 years old,

01:23:50.520 --> 01:23:52.520
he tells him this thing about him.

01:23:52.520 --> 01:23:57.520
He was happy to be that he was telling that particular passage,

01:23:57.520 --> 01:24:02.520
but was explained to him by a Yamanali.

01:24:02.520 --> 01:24:06.520
The other curiosity man says, I want to answer him the question.

01:24:06.520 --> 01:24:10.520
He answers the little boy, what is the meaning of the passage?

01:24:10.520 --> 01:24:18.520
On the spot, as you said, he tells us exactly the meaning that the Yamanavi had revealed to them.

01:24:19.520 --> 01:24:22.520
Now Ma'an is perplexed, he doesn't know what to do.

01:24:23.520 --> 01:24:28.520
The problem is not with the Mishnah, the problem is with what the Yamanavi had told us.

01:24:28.520 --> 01:24:32.520
One minute.

01:24:32.520 --> 01:24:39.520
Goes back to his room, to his home, again, and now when I leave the room, he says,

01:24:39.520 --> 01:24:47.520
Manatu, I have a question. You have told me something, but this interpretation was inherent,

01:24:47.520 --> 01:24:51.720
concerned with the scope of human reasoning

01:24:51.720 --> 01:24:55.520
and behold I discovered a boy, 6-7 years old

01:24:55.520 --> 01:24:58.720
and he came and said this to me

01:24:58.720 --> 01:25:01.020
what's the meaning of this?

01:25:01.020 --> 01:25:02.820
the Aravind says

01:25:02.820 --> 01:25:05.020
but I told you this truth

01:25:05.020 --> 01:25:08.320
the meaning of that which I was told to you today

01:25:08.320 --> 01:25:11.020
but once that you discover it

01:25:11.020 --> 01:25:15.420
it becomes accessible to every single human being

01:25:15.420 --> 01:25:29.420
That is not math. The famous theories, relativity of Einstein, Newton's law of gravity, convertibles and others became accessible to every human being now.

01:25:29.420 --> 01:25:38.420
Our little boys now they are studying relativity. For us it is difficult to understand the alphabet, not to the little boys, because they are part of their own make-up.

01:25:38.420 --> 01:25:40.420
You know?

01:25:40.420 --> 01:25:42.420
That is Chokmah.

01:25:42.420 --> 01:25:44.420
Alright.

01:25:44.420 --> 01:25:46.420
What is Binahim?

01:25:46.420 --> 01:25:48.420
Very simple.

01:25:48.420 --> 01:25:50.420
Chokmah,

01:25:50.420 --> 01:25:52.420
he conceived things in abstract.

01:25:52.420 --> 01:25:54.420
Take Einstein.

01:25:54.420 --> 01:25:56.420
The splitting of the atom.

01:25:56.420 --> 01:25:58.420
Understand very well.

01:25:58.420 --> 01:26:00.420
Fusion. Atomic fusion.

01:26:00.420 --> 01:26:02.420
This is the Chakab.

01:26:02.420 --> 01:26:04.420
Binahim,

01:26:04.420 --> 01:26:06.420
he knows to apply it

01:26:06.420 --> 01:26:09.920
make electricity out of it.

01:26:09.920 --> 01:26:14.020
Einstein probably would have been incapable

01:26:14.020 --> 01:26:18.020
of making, I don't know, an atomic plant.

01:26:19.520 --> 01:26:22.720
He was not an engineer.

01:26:22.720 --> 01:26:24.820
The engineer, in other words, is not a god.

01:26:24.820 --> 01:26:27.020
He just thought that all the principles

01:26:27.020 --> 01:26:29.420
are discovered by others.

01:26:29.420 --> 01:26:32.120
You see, there is a scientist, the original thinker,

01:26:32.120 --> 01:26:34.420
who wins the Nobel Prize.

01:26:34.420 --> 01:26:46.420
And then the physicians or doctors or whatever it is who apply that principle in practical, concrete things. That is Vinaya.

01:26:48.420 --> 01:26:56.420
And what is that? That is the knowledge that we gain through common experience.

01:26:56.420 --> 01:27:07.420
not through intellectual thinking, not because you read a book, but because you put a thought, but through your daily experience.

01:27:07.420 --> 01:27:14.420
Empirical wisdom that you gain as you grow and you live.

01:27:14.420 --> 01:27:18.420
The first thing you ask for God, Da'at.

01:27:18.420 --> 01:27:28.420
Even the Da'at, the common experience, comes from you.

01:27:28.420 --> 01:27:38.420
Where ability of assimilating, synthesizing, common experiences of Da'at comes from you.

01:27:38.420 --> 01:27:43.840
Mithlika khukhmah binah bada'ah.

01:27:43.840 --> 01:27:46.840
Wa l-ghaftaa al-shayr, wa l-manta'ah.

01:27:46.840 --> 01:27:48.840
Clear the first expression?

01:27:48.840 --> 01:27:50.840
Alright.

